Three contract workers died on Monday at a factory owned by Indian Apple supplier Tata Electronics, reports <em><a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/india/three-workers-die-tata-electronics-iphone-parts-plant-new-indian-express-reports-2026-11-10/">Reuters</a></em>. The facility in Hosur, Tamil Nadu, manufactures components for the iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2020/08/apple-india.jpg" alt="" width="2304" height="1296" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-756076" /><br/>
The workers were performing maintenance at a wastewater treatment plant at the Tata facility when they inhaled gas while inspecting a nano-filtration tank. The plant was operated by Nalco Water, and the workers were employed by a subcontractor.<br/>
<br/>
Apple, Tata Electronics, and state officials will look into the incident, with Apple sending a "team" to assist in the investigation.<br/>
<br/>
The incident did not affect iPhone production because the facility was closed for Diwali.<br/>
<br/>
